course: dictionary
lesson: 15348
title: Caring words: solicitous
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Solicitous is a formal word, the kind you meet in stories and exam papers. It means caring about someone and paying close attention to how they are.
explain: «The nurse was solicitous and checked on him every hour.» The clue is checked on him every hour. She watches over him closely because she cares, so solicitous means caring and attentive.
explain: The word can also mean eager or anxious to do something. «He was solicitous to please his teacher» means he was very keen to make sure she was happy with his work.
fact: Solicitous means caring and attentive, or eager to do something.
fact: «Solicitous» is a formal word, so you will mostly meet it in stories and exam papers.
fact: Useful phrases are «solicitous of» someone and «solicitous about» something, as in «solicitous about my cold».
fact: The adverb is solicitously, as in «She asked solicitously how I felt.»
fact: In everyday speech, you can swap in caring or attentive to check your meaning.
exercise: «The nurse was solicitous and checked on him every hour.» What does solicitous mean? | Bored and tired | Angry and loud | *Caring and watching over someone closely | Forgetful
exercise: «He was solicitous to please his teacher.» What does solicitous suggest here? | Lazy and slow | *Eager to make sure he did well | Afraid of his teacher | Keen to go home early
exercise: «The shop assistant asked solicitously if we needed help.» What does solicitously mean? | Rudely | Very quickly | In a whisper | *In a caring, attentive way
test: «Aunt Rose was solicitous about my cold, so she made me hot soup.» What does solicitous mean? | Lost in thought | Loud and cheerful | *Caring and anxious about my health | Bored
test: Jess says solicitous means bossy, so it must be rude. What is the best answer? | Yes, bossy means the same as rude | It means very quiet | It means very tired | *No, it means caring and attentive, which is kind
exam: In «He was solicitous of his grandmother's comfort», what does solicitous mean? | Careless about | *Caring about and attentive to | Afraid of | Angry with
